{"step_index":1035,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-10-19T17:46:04Z","input_tokens":3155,"cache_read_tokens":132215,"output_tokens":1070,"thinking":"Defining two distinct operational modes: Crypto and Prop Firm Futures, distinguished by the 'MarketCategory' parameter. Crypto mode necessitates an initial balance of $42 and a portfolio comprising SOL, BTC, ETH, and meme coins. Prop Firm mode requires an initial balance of $50,000, a profit target of $3,000, and a trailing drawdown limit of $2,000.\n\n\nConsidering the multi-agent system, the \"Hermes\" agent is the central decision-maker. It synthesizes inputs from \"Atlas\" (macro bias), \"Lumen\" (economic news), \"Hydra\" (setup score), \"Sentinel\" (risk), \"Hephaestus\" (order proposal), and \"Mnemosyne\" (performance).  When in \"HITL_MANUAL\" mode, Hermes enters a `pendingApproval` state, requiring human confirmation before trade execution.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"view_file","args":{"AbsolutePath":"\"/Users/dev/Documents/Antigravity/grok-bot-dashboard/src/engine/simulationData.ts\"","toolAction":"\"Viewing simulationData.ts\"","toolSummary":"\"View simulationData.ts\""}}]}
